      * ZS104A: Gregorian epoch/century/leap and upper date limits
      * SPEC: INTEGER-OF-DATE/DATE-OF-INTEGER/DAY-OF-INTEGER; S05.
      * EXPECTED SERIAL = GREGORIAN DAYS SINCE 1601-01-01 PLUS 1.
      * 1900 AND 2100 ARE COMMON YEARS; 2000 IS A LEAP YEAR.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. ZS104A.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO REPORT.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  REPORT-FILE
           RECORDING MODE F
           RECORD CONTAINS 120 CHARACTERS.
       01  REPORT-RECORD PIC X(120).
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
           COPY ZCVSRPT.
       01  WS-DATE PIC 9(8).
       01  WS-DAY PIC 9(7).
       01  WS-N PIC 9(9) COMP.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PROC SECTION.
       MAIN-000.
           MOVE 'ZS104A' TO ZCVS-PROG-ID.
           PERFORM ZCVS-BEGIN.

           MOVE 'DATE-16010101' TO ZCVS-TEST-NAME.
           COMPUTE WS-N = FUNCTION INTEGER-OF-DATE(16010101).
           COMPUTE WS-DATE = FUNCTION DATE-OF-INTEGER(WS-N).
           COMPUTE WS-DAY = FUNCTION DAY-OF-INTEGER(WS-N).
           IF WS-N = 1 AND WS-DATE = 16010101
             AND WS-DAY = 1601001
               PERFORM ZCVS-PASS
           ELSE
               MOVE '1' TO ZCVS-EXPECTED
               MOVE WS-N TO ZCVS-ACTUAL
               PERFORM ZCVS-FAIL
           END-IF.

